  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "The former Philips estate De Wielewaal became a public legacy of Marc Brouwers, the Dutch businessman who bought and renovated its house. He sold the estate to Eindhoven in 2022, welcoming the prospect of residents exploring a place long closed to them. The city planned to join its woods with surrounding green spaces and ruled out housing development.\n\nIndustrial property provided another outlet for Brouwers’s capital. Through Maja Investments, he participated alongside VolkerWessels in Brainport Industries Campus, a complex designed for advanced manufacturing and related education. The partners sold the campus to Capreon in 2020. Its combination of production facilities, businesses and training institutions placed his property investment within Eindhoven’s wider industrial economy.",
    "html": "<p>The former Philips estate De Wielewaal became a public legacy of Marc Brouwers, the Dutch businessman who bought and renovated its house. He sold the estate to Eindhoven in 2022, welcoming the prospect of residents exploring a place long closed to them. The city planned to join its woods with surrounding green spaces and ruled out housing development.</p>\r\n<p>Industrial property provided another outlet for Brouwers’s capital. Through Maja Investments, he participated alongside VolkerWessels in Brainport Industries Campus, a complex designed for advanced manufacturing and related education. The partners sold the campus to Capreon in 2020. Its combination of production facilities, businesses and training institutions placed his property investment within Eindhoven’s wider industrial economy.</p>\r\n",
